## Session bootstrap (recommended)

1. Read [LAYOUT.md](LAYOUT.md).  
2. Skim this file and [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).  
3. If shared graph/RAG (or other platform services) are configured for this lab,
   **validate them before asserting live status** (health endpoint, MCP, or
   documented probe). Do not invent “healthy” from memory.  
4. Prefer work on a feature or session branch — never commit secrets.

## Monorepo layout (read first)

```text
products/   → ship code
services/   → shared platform services
hosts/      → IaC
lab/        → experiments (never ship as-is)
docs/       → durable knowledge
workspace/  → scratch only
```

```bash
python3 scripts/print_layout.py
```

Do **not** invent top-level directories. Put durable notes in `docs/`, not
`workspace/`.

## neo-harness (if embedded)

Constrained PLAN→ACT→REFLECT jobs use the workspace runner (not a global
`neo` assumed on PATH):

```bash
./scripts/neo doctor
./scripts/neo start --task-file jobs/<slug>.md --agent workspace -p mock
```

- Install/refresh: project `.venv-neo` + `requirements-neo.txt` (or editable neo-harness)  
- Docs: [starting-a-workspace](https://github.com/westailabs/neo-harness/blob/master/docs/starting-a-workspace.md)  
- Upstream: https://github.com/westailabs/neo-harness  

## Shared services (generic stub)

If this monorepo documents shared retrieval or knowledge-graph services:

| Rule | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| Before asserting status | Probe health / live query |
| If unreachable | Say so; continue only with local offline work |
